{
  "contract": "native-schema-slices.md revision 4",
  "slice": "2c",
  "setup": {
    "notes": [
      "Runs as UID 1000 in the disposable probe VM; the probe's private directory contains an empty directory 'mnt'",
      "child E calls unshare(CLONE_NEWUSER | CLONE_NEWNS), then mounts tmpfs 'ant-tmpfs' on 'mnt' with MS_NOSUID|MS_NODEV and options taken from a page-aligned 4096-byte buffer holding 'size=1m,mode=0700', then exits",
      "mount.unprivileged passes NULL data, so no data field is recorded",
      "mount.boundary_options places 'mode=0700' plus NUL padding in the last 16 bytes of a readable page followed by a PROT_NONE page",
      "quotactl cases use the missing block device '/dev/ant-missing'; quotaon names the missing quota file 'aquota.user'; xquotaon passes flags 1; xgetqstatv passes qs_version 1",
      "quotactl_fd cases use a descriptor for the probe's /tmp directory (initramfs root), which has no quota operations (ENOSYS); setquota passes an if_dqblk with dqb_bhardlimit 1",
      "kexec_load passes one segment {buf 'ANTINOMIE-KEXEC', bufsz 15, mem 0x1000000, memsz 4096} and is rejected for lacking CAP_SYS_BOOT; too_many passes 17 segments",
      "rseq cases use glibc's registered area (thread pointer + __rseq_offset) with length 32 (ORIG_RSEQ_SIZE, the length glibc registers) and RSEQ_SIG 0x53053053; register_again and unregister_badsig run on the main thread; the dedicated rseq thread unregisters and immediately registers again"
    ]
  },
